  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows negative sentiment (e.g., -0.25 or 0.00) and true prices show strong downward momentum.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoot after sharp price spikes (e.g., >70% above recent high) by applying a 10-15% dampening factor.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is >10% above 30-day moving average, reduce by 5-10% for next period.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent low prices when sentiment is neutral or positive (e.g., 0.00) and prices are trending down.",
    "For horizon >15 days, reduce forecast volatility by 20-30% if sentiment is flat or negative, to avoid overreaction to short-term noise.",
    "When true price drops below 65.00 after a spike, adjust forecast downward by 5-10% to reflect potential mean reversion or policy-induced cooling."
  ]
